  "finding": "B: the exact search gives mu(2) = 3 and mu(3) = 6 (the n=3 minimum is proved, not estimated: every choice of five rank-1 matrices was tried). Composed by Karatsuba to n=12 that is 54 ANDs against the built-in 63, i.e. 14.3% fewer, and the composed algorithm reproduces the field product on 200 sampled inputs with 0 mismatches.  A: deleting every region that still runs unconditionally is worth at most 94,470 static Toffolis (2.71% of the arm's emitted stream, and executed <= static), so a predicate discoverer has that much to find here and no more.  C: the multiply is most of the gap but not all of it. The arm decomposes exactly as 536,980.0 Toffoli of non-multiply work plus 10,510 executed calls of a multiply that costs its AND count plus 12, so at the proved 6-AND base the arm would execute 1,230,640.0 per shot; even a 23-AND multiply -- the 2n-1 dimension bound, which this repository has no characteristic-2 construction for -- leaves 904,830.0 (2.03x the 445,229 target), and a multiply that cost nothing but its 12-Toffoli add still leaves 663,100.0 (1.49x the target). So no multiply, however cheap, delivers the target on this decoder: the 536,980.0 that is not the multiply has to shrink too, which is an algorithm change."
